course: dictionary
lesson: 13288
title: Grammarian
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: A word can tell you a lot about a person before you read the rest. The ending «-ian» often means someone connected with something: a musician makes music, and a magician does magic. So a grammarian is connected with grammar.
explain: «Ms Okafor is a grammarian who writes books about how English sentences are built.» Grammar is the set of rules for how words and sentences are put together. A grammarian is an expert on those rules, or writes about them. Try swapping in «an expert on grammar» and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: People also use grammarian in everyday talk, in a playful way. «My sister is a grammar fan: she always corrects my commas.» She is not writing books. She cares a lot about correct grammar and likes to point out mistakes. Look at the words around the word to see which meaning is used.
fact: Grammar means the rules of how words and sentences are built in a language.
fact: «Grammarian» means a person who studies grammar, or who writes books about it.
fact: Informal: «grammarian» can also mean someone who cares a lot about correct grammar.
fact: «Ancient grammarians» were early experts who described how a language worked, long before modern school books existed.
fact: Pāṇini was an ancient Indian grammarian who wrote very detailed rules for the language Sanskrit.
exercise: «Ms Okafor is a grammarian who writes books about how English sentences are built.» What is a grammarian? | A person who cannot speak any language | A word for a very old castle | *A person who studies grammar or writes about it | A person who bakes bread for the village
exercise: Mum says, «You are a real grammarian, you corrected my spelling again.» What does grammarian mean in this sentence? | A type of bird that lives by the sea | Someone who grows vegetables in the garden | *Someone who cares a lot about correct grammar | A loud noise made by a drum
exercise: «The ancient grammarians wrote rules for their language long before school books existed.» Find and copy the one word that tells you they lived long ago. | rules | *ancient | wrote | grammarians
test: «The grammarian checked every sentence in the book for mistakes.» What is the grammarian most likely doing? | *Studying and correcting the rules of how sentences are built | Running a race around the playground | Cooking dinner for the whole class | Painting pictures of the sentences on the wall
test: Ben says, «Stop being such a grammarian, nobody cares about that comma!» What does Ben mean? | You are a famous writer of stories | You have lost your pencil case | You are a fast runner | *You are too fussy about correct grammar
exam: Which sentence uses grammarian correctly? | *The grammarian explained why «who» and «whom» are used in different places. | The grammarian was a loud clap of thunder over the hills. | The grammarian grew tomatoes and carrots in the garden. | We ate a grammarian for lunch at school today.
